        "id": 1101726
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-07T20:57:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we really need to gate this by OS version?\n\nWe can probably be optimistic that apps will adapt to this across their code base when they target V regardless of the OS they are running on.\n\nI think it might be worth simplifying this -- how hard is it to plumb the \"true\" blocked status even when the API relies on NPMS?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2336,
        "startChar": 40,
        "endLine": 2336,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "9d8f7e26e71ed4bb07d9ce2aae36193013892025",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fdfabe78_df01a492",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 2336,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T06:30:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So you\u0027re saying that this code should return BLOCKED even on pre-V if the app doesn\u0027t have the internet permission?\n\nI think that\u0027s harder because the checks are spread between multiple methods, and the existing code only has a way to ignore blocked status and doesn\u0027t have a way to force blocked status, and there\u0027s complications such as legacy lockdown. The best I can come up with is:\n\n    final boolean hasInternetPermission \u003d (mBpfNetMaps.getNetPermForUid(uid) \u0026 PERMISSION_INTERNET) !\u003d 0;\n    final boolean blockedByNoInternet \u003d !hasInternetPermission \u0026\u0026 mDeps.isChangeEnabled(\n            NETWORKINFO_WITHOUT_INTERNET_BLOCKED, uid);\n\n    final NetworkInfo networkInfo \u003d getFilteredNetworkInfo(nai, uid, !blockedByNoInternet);\n    if (blockedByNoInternet) {\n        networkInfo.setDetailedState(DetailedState.BLOCKED, null /* reason */,\n                null /* extraInfo */);\n    }\n\nIt\u0027s not super easy to read, but maybe it\u0027s OK. Or maybe we could add an extra forceBlocked parameter to filterNetworkInfo.\n\nMotomu, what do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "f341ea6b_79028ae4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2336,
        "startChar": 40,
        "endLine": 2336,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "9d8f7e26e71ed4bb07d9ce2aae36193013892025",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da55b637_e0c69850",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 2336,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T07:27:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it\u0027s easy to do on pre-V.\nIt\u0027s possible that BpfNetMaps#isUidNetworkingBlocked returns false for app without INTERNET if no allowlist firewall chains is enabled.\nSo, it\u0027s not easy to keep the behavior consistent between U- and V+ with compat flag enabled.\nI prefer to keep the current behavior on U- and change the behavior only on V+.",
      "parentUuid": "f341ea6b_79028ae4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2336,
        "startChar": 40,
        "endLine": 2336,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "9d8f7e26e71ed4bb07d9ce2aae36193013892025",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "801269dd_23f68842",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 2336,
      "author": {
        "id": 1101726
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T08:03:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wait, so you mean we can still return `true` from isConnected when INTERNET permission is missing even on V+?\n\nI\u0027d say then it is better to fix the whole thing at this time. No INTERNET permission does forbid networking at some layer, right? So we must signal that in NetworkInfo somehow, no matter what is going on with the firewalls. And ideally that thing should be consistent across OS versions after this mainline update.\n\nIt is an acceptable argument that the complexity is prohibitive, in that case we can leave it as a TODO bug for later.",
      "parentUuid": "da55b637_e0c69850",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2336,
        "startChar": 40,
        "endLine": 2336,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "9d8f7e26e71ed4bb07d9ce2aae36193013892025",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a54bd4d_75fae80f",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 2336,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T12:18:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think BpfNetMaps#isUidNetworkingBlocked was implemented as a replacement of NetworkPolicyManager#isUidNetworkingBlocked originally.\nSo this method only checks the firewall chain status and does not check app\u0027s permission.\n\nI agree that we should say network is blocked for apps without INTERNET permission.\nwe may want to define BLOCKED_REASON for lack of internet permission.\nFor this CL, I have updated isNetworkWithCapabilitiesBlocked to check app\u0027s permission on V+.",
      "parentUuid": "801269dd_23f68842",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2336,
        "startChar": 40,
        "endLine": 2336,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "9d8f7e26e71ed4bb07d9ce2aae36193013892025",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
